axiom_user_va_limit	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
# Armv8.3 PAuth (the identity on x86_64): authenticating a signed plain
# user address with the same modifier gives it back. Isla checks the
# aarch64 round trip in every configuration verus/isla/seams.md names;
# firmware's key enables and other CPUs stay outside the runs.
axiom_auth_sign	platform/kernel fact	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: that firmware sets SCR_EL3.API and APK and that the CPU is one of the two kinds the runs model)
# Inline assembly checked with Isla (verus/ISLA.md): run.sh checks each
# against the contract verus/isla/seams.md quotes. `spec_sign` and
# `spec_auth` are one function per process only while the kernel keeps
# the thread's data key A and EnDA as they were, which the runs take as
# given, and an `autda` that faults returns only if the kernel resumes
# past it.
sign	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: that the kernel keeps the thread's data key A and EnDA fixed)
auth	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: that the kernel keeps the thread's data key A and EnDA fixed and never resumes past an autda that faults)
strip	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: that firmware sets SCR_EL3.API and APK and that the CPU is one of the two kinds the runs model)
